2026-07-15T03:03:10.819179+00:00	QM_STUDY_PREREG 2026-07-14: spec sha256 eac27f5743267500ff59e01b75f33837c96bfdfd5fb32c1e0c06a824f537f1cb at commit 5bf97f2. Owner-typed values (typed in owner session message 2026-07-14, entered at owner direction): QM_RUN_LOOKBACK=60 QM_RUN_MIN_PCT=0.30 QM_BASE_MIN_DAYS=10 QM_BASE_MAX_DAYS=40 QM_BASE_MAX_DEPTH=0.20 QM_BASE_SMA=20 QM_VOL_DRYUP_RATIO=0.65 QM_PARA_LOOKBACK=20 QM_PARA_MIN_PCT=0.50 QM_PARA_GREEN_DAYS=3 QM_PARA_EXT_PCT=0.15 QM_PARA_SMA=20 QM_HORIZONS=(5,10,20) QM_TRADABILITY_DTE=(30,60) QM_NTM_BAND=0.10. Horizons frozen. Excess return = signal-forward return minus the same name's unconditional same-length baseline (post-hoc-universe defense). Stage 1 = counts-only feasibility: a setup with fewer than 10 deduped fires across the universe is untestable-as-specified; 10-19 deduped fires = descriptive report only, can never justify an H8 arc; recalibration on counts alone requires a logged QM_STUDY_PREREG_V2 and never uses outcome information. Pre-declared counts-only fallback ladder (still requires V2 fact): too few parabolic fires -> QM_PARA_EXT_PCT 0.15->0.10 (keep 0.50/20-session run); too few breakout fires -> QM_BASE_MAX_DEPTH 0.20->0.25 (keep 0.30 prior run). Stage 2 = ONE full study run per data vintage; re-runs on new data are new dated reports; threshold changes require a new preregistration fact. Pre-registered readings, per setup and direction-specific to each setup's source claim: BREAKOUT (long continuation) justifies drafting a separate H8 preregistration only if all of: >=20 deduped fires; median forward excess return > 0 at >=2 of the 3 horizons; the 20-session horizon is among the positive ones; fire-session tradability >= 60%. No H8 for breakout if any of: <20 deduped fires; median excess <= 0 at >=2 horizons; median excess at 20 sessions <= 0; tradability < 60%. PARABOLIC (fade -- signal-only per spec section 3) justifies drafting a separate H8 preregistration only if all of: >=20 deduped fires; median forward excess return < 0 at >=2 of the 3 horizons; the 5-session horizon is among the negative ones (a snapback is a short-horizon claim); fire-session tradability >= 60%. No H8 for parabolic if any of: <20 deduped fires; median excess >= 0 at >=2 horizons; median excess at 5 sessions >= 0; tradability < 60%. Provenance note: the parabolic direction clause is LLM-ADJUSTED pre-outcome (agent, 2026-07-14 session, before any counts or returns were viewed): the owner draft applied the long-side reading to both setups; parabolic is a fade signal per the spec, so the long-side reading could never deliver that setup's motivating conclusion. All other values and rules are owner-typed. Passing these rules supports further testing only; it does not authorize execution, sizing, live orders, or threshold changes. Universe = h7_scope.watch_universe() at run time; thin history reads as thin.
2026-07-15T03:05:54.766473+00:00	QM_STUDY_RESULT 2026-07-14: one full run per QM_STUDY_PREREG 2026-07-14, data vintage 2026-07-14, report reports/2026-07-14-qm-base-rates.md. Stage 1 counts: breakout 11 deduped fires (10-19 band -> descriptive only, no H8 decision possible); parabolic 35 deduped fires (>=20 -> H8 rules apply). No V2 recalibration used. Stage 2 pooled readings (per-fire forward return minus same-name unconditional baseline median, pooled median across universe): BREAKOUT +5d +0.02% / +10d +4.18% / +20d +3.29%, tradability 4/7 = 57.1% (below the 60% gate; moot given the counts band). PARABOLIC +5d +2.68% / +10d +0.70% / +20d +1.47% -- POSITIVE at all three horizons; tradability 18/19 = 94.7%. Pre-registered decisions: BREAKOUT descriptive only (counts band), no H8. PARABOLIC fade reading REJECTED (median excess >= 0 at >=2 horizons and at the 5-session horizon): parabolic fires preceded better-than-baseline continuation, not a snapback, in this hindsight-selected sample. NO H8 arc for either setup. Disclosed: under the owner draft's long-side reading the parabolic numbers would have crossed the justifies-H8 line; that direction was corrected pre-outcome to match the setup's fade claim, and adopting a long-continuation reading NOW would be post-hoc -- it would need a new preregistration on unseen forward data. Small samples (11 and 35 correlated fires, one dominant regime); no execution, sizing, or live-order implication.
